"Bless me Anhur, for I have sinned; it has been ten days since my last
Ascension."

Short desc: my 7th ascension; 3rd Wizard; 2nd genoless; 1st wishless.
Ascended knowing all 40 spells.  Pretended to be an extinctionist for a
while, but still ended up with not many points.

Long story:

I started on a whim, and didn't seem to have a bunch of neat stuff.  19 Int
and 12 Wis, good.  But wand of digging, +1 ring of increase accuracy, +3
increase damage, detect monsters, a harp (as opposed to horn or drum), potions
of sickness and paralysis.  Nothing too exciting.  I went ahead anyway.

Things started looking good quickly.  "Hey, what's this diagonal passage.  Oh
look, a dwarf.  Mew, he's got your mittens!" <slash>  He'd already raised the
vault, so I got the gold and his pick-axe.

Soon I spent the gold, since level 2 had a giant bookshop, and level 3 ahd a
good general store, I think with a magic lamp.

I rose in level, then I got mew to become a large cat.  Killed some sort of
naga and felt healthy.  Ate a floating eye, but had no blindfolding, so I
started casting detect monster a fair bit.  Regular practice with a 1st level
divination spell?  Hey...

I went into the Mines, and right there found a bones of someone else's wizard,
killed by a white unicorn.  with Magicbane, some spellbooks, a lot of boots, a
wand of polymorph, and a magic marker.  Everything interesting was cursed, of
course, but I figured life was good.  If I could kill the unicorn -- he
wouldn't let me line him up for a force bolt, unless I went next to him, at
which point he'd take off half my hit points and I'd engrave Elbereth with my
digging and whimper.  Eventually I found some spot near a corner where if I
didn't move neither would he -- no trap, and quite some distance away, but
almost as if the algorithm couldn't find a place to jump him to.  I couldn't
touch him, but mew could, and soon I had a unicorn horn.

Then mew turned into an ettin zombie and was abandoned due to impatience.
I found a wand of death, but ended up emptying it and the wand of digging in
Not Dying due to soldier ants and other things.  I'd engrave Elbereth, then
kill something dead, and so forth.

Minetown had a bag of tricks and a bag of holding for sale, and a cross altar.
Kept on going, to the Wine Cellar.  Another dwarf fetched the gems for me.
Nothing too exciting happend.  Found a touchstone, and I guess some holy water
-- got to bless the bag at some point.  And a scroll of charging.  Eventually
I realized I'd started with a blessed scroll of remove curse and uncursed all
the bones stuff.  Boots turned out to be jumping, water walking, and speed.

I tried polymorphing the bookshop owner; it didn't work.  But he wasted his
time zapping magic missile and striking at my cloak, while I hit him.  He
died.  Learned detect treasure, magic mapping.  Had two spellbooks of detect
treasure, diluted one, wrote identify.  Bought up books from the general
store, diluted protection (one of the more useless spells) and wrote magic
missile.  Later found charm monster, to found out the essentials, and light
and create monster.

I realized I was actually getting to play like a wizard -- detect monster
instead of ESP (though later I got a towel), detect treasure early enough to
be useful, plus of course identify...

Found a 2nd bones in the dungeon, only interesting thing there were gauntlets
of dexterity.

Found a graveyard, lured the wraiths upstairs, got up to level 15.  Went
questing, read a scroll of reverse genocide, sent in some wraiths, went up to
level 17.  Time to eat a tengu.

