no body armor!  cloak, helm 2, gloves, speed.

Around this point I realized that I hadn't used any wishes, and that I didn't
really need to.  The most urgent thing to wish for is MR, which wizards have
rather well covered.  Generic DSM you can make; reflection is relatively easy
to find, I had speed boots and holding... suddenly wishless conduct didn't
seem so impossible.

Killed the Dark One with handly teleportation, found a cornuthaum, switched to
it for style and clairvoyance although my AC got worse.  Got crowned at his
private altar.

altars on 7, 12, 13, 15.  Got Frost Brand, made it +7 and used it for much of
the game.

Ludios was on 18.  With 3 black dragons.  I ran away.

Got a shield of reflection off an Angel, which turned my casting failure from
0 to 72%.  Dumped it.

If I'd kept on going I'd have found dragons in a zoo, but I lost patience and
wrote a scroll of cursed genocide and sent in some silver dragons.  Standing
on the upstairs, because I figured they were immune to anything I could throw
at them.  (Maybe not -- skilled fireball, or broken wands of sleep...)  Killed
one, ran off with the scales, and soon had the classic silver DSM *without* a
wish... at least, a "real" wish; cursed genocide felt a bit like cheating.

Cleared out Ludios.

Found a temple of Anhur, got more protection (already had Stealth and
spontanoues protection from praying.)  Found Medusa, left her alone, jumped up
to level 1 and went down casting magic mapping and detect treasure
systematically.  Found some rooms I'd completely missed, including a temple to
Thoth on 9.

Crossed Medusa and the Castle with water walking, and had left my jumping
boots behind, so I couldn't loot there storerooms then.  

I bounced up and down between Gehennom and my altar on 15, alternating between
the descent/map/detect cycle and long sac fests courtesy of create monster.  I
got lots of spellbooks -- eventually I learned all 40 spells.  I'd been going
polyless, despite that bones wand, but caved in after I got a spellbook of
polymorph.  Got cool rings -- conflict, slow dig, poly control -- which I
never used, and scrolls of enchant armor.  No magic whistles, no more magic
markers.

